1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,670
Would you really do the same thing
in that situation, teach?!

2
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:09,500
Some pain in life must be 
borne with. Remember that.

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,540
Stupid freshman like you 
don't get to talk back!

4
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,710
Eat shit and die!

5
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:15,380
Hold on, Kite!

6
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:16,580
Stay out of it.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,830
He's doing exactly what 
Satsuki told us we'd have to.

8
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:21,830
For real.

9
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:25,960
Right now, he's bearing all the pain
so that the basketball team can survive.

10
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,210
Kite...

11
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:28,630
That dumbass!

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,500
And it's our responsibility...

13
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:33,920
...to bear the pain of having
to watch him get beat up like this!

14
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:35,630
But honestly...

15
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:39,540
...I don't think this whole "bear the pain" thing
is such a good fit for me.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,080
So without further ado, I'll be introducing
the newest member of the team.

17
00:00:45,330 --> 00:00:45,920
Natsume Kenj-

18
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,040
I'm Kite.

19
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,330
I look forward to playing with you.

20
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:49,960
I get it.

21
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:52,210
I'm done. No more fights.

22
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:55,130
Still, our practice sessions have only been
the same thing over and over.

23
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,580
Don't you have anything else 
that we can do, Captain?

24
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,000
Yo, Teach.

25
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,750
Quit staring and try actually 
coaching us for once.

26
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,330
You're our advisor, right?

27
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,580
That's true.

28
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:07,460
Then... how about you do some running?

29
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:13,580
Dammit, Momoharu. You and your big fat mouth.

30
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:15,960
Um, Momoharu?

31
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:20,500
I think we really need someone to help research
and plan a training schedule for us.

32
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:23,500
You're right. I'll think about it.

33
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:40,960
Rikukaikuu doko ni ikou

34
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:43,420
Ahiru no Sora

35
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:44,000
Kimi o sasoitai na

36
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:48,880
Monogatari wa hajima tterunda

37
00:01:51,210 --> 00:01:54,580
Okubyou kaze mo recycle

38
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:57,580
Mayotteru senaka oshite

39
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:02,790
Give and go! Isogou

40
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:10,920
Mogutteita honou ga kaodashite

41
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:18,130
Kakusenai no sa yume ni mita yume

42
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,540
Tobenai tsubasa demo

43
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:28,420
Bokura wa habataite sora o kanjitai

44
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,750
Naritai jibun ni naritai

45
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:38,420
Ima dekinai koto mo ashita wa wakannai ze

46
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:41,880
Waru agaki shiyou

47
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:44,920
Happy go ducky!

48
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:59,920
Manager

49
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,130
Yasu! You need to be more 
aggressive on defense!

50
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,830
You've left him wide open for a three!

51
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:04,830
R-right!

52
00:03:24,670 --> 00:03:25,290
Huh?

53
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:27,790
What was that?

54
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,670
What's wrong? You hurt or something?

55
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:36,170
No, but I heard a weird 
noise from my sneakers...

56
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:42,080
M-m-my basketball shoes... 
have a hole in them!!

57
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:51,040
Nasuko South
Shopping District

58
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,750
Sports Shop
Suzuki

59
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,750
Hmm... this hole is bad news.

60
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:56,830
I think it'd be faster if you just bought
an entirely new pair.

61
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:59,460
Sports Shop
Suzuki

62
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,380
These are an older model, anyway.

63
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,460
Are you sure?

64
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:01,420
Um...

65
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:02,790
How about these babies?

66
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:05,710
They're a new model from AND1.
Buy them now and I'll hook you up with a discount.

67
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:07,830
Um, no thanks, I'm good.

68
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,210
This totally sucks...

69
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:16,420
I've been to 5 stores already
and none were willing to fix them for me.

70
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:21,540
Crap! The next shop is the 
very last one on my list!

71
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:25,460
Sports Nanao

72
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,170
Whatever.

73
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:25,460
If this place won't do it,
then I'll just have to fix them myself.

74
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,500
Right here. This is it.

75
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,460
NANAO

76
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,420
Excuse me!

77
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:39,920
Hello?

78
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:44,000
Whoa. They have a lot more
basketball stuff than I expected.

79
00:04:44,330 --> 00:04:45,960
That might be a good sign!

80
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:46,670
Coming!

81
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,210
Welcome!

82
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,460
Please wait a moment!

83
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:08,380
Ow, that hurt!

84
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:10,830
Huh? Where's the customer?

85
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:12,880
U-um...

86
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:16,250
I... can't breathe...

87
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,880
I'm sorry! So Sorry!

88
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:26,630
I was in such a rush I lost my footing.
Please forgive me!

89
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:28,420
It's okay. I'm sorry, too.

90
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:30,500
Um, you're not hurt, are you?

91
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,540
Uh, no!

92
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:33,170
I'm totally fine thanks to you!

93
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:35,540
Huh?

94
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:37,920
You're Kurumatani!

95
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:41,000
Um... have we met before?

96
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,250
I actually go to the same school as you!

97
00:05:43,830 --> 00:05:46,040
Oh! You're in the class next to mine...

98
00:05:47,830 --> 00:05:50,380
I'm so glad that you remember me!

99
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:51,790
Uh, yeah.

100
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:55,460
You stood out to me at the first school assembly,
since we're about the same height.

101
00:05:57,170 --> 00:05:58,210
That's for sure!

102
00:05:58,210 --> 00:06:00,130
My name is Nao Nanao!

103
00:06:00,670 --> 00:06:01,710
Let's be friends!

104
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,330
I'm Sora Kurumatani.

105
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,630
Very cute...

106
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,330
What?

107
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:10,080
Huh?! Oh, uh, nothing! Never mind!

108
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:13,960
Um, so, I came here hoping 
to get these fixed...

109
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:14,880
Sure.

110
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:21,920
Can you wait a sec?

111
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:26,040
My dad knows way more about 
doing repairs than I do.

112
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,420
So I'm gonna go and get him.

113
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:31,580
Ouch!

114
00:06:32,330 --> 00:06:35,210
U-uh oh, I'm starting to 
sense a pattern here...

115
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,210
I'm sorry.

116
00:06:40,630 --> 00:06:43,580
It seems like my dad is 
away for the time being.

117
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:46,880
Would you mind just leaving 
your shoes here with us?

118
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:47,750
Okay.

119
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:54,750
But even from an amateur 
perspective like mine...

120
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:58,000
I can tell you might be better 
off with an entirely new pair.

121
00:06:58,170 --> 00:07:01,040
These days there are a bunch
of different models on the market.

122
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,750
You can easily get a decent 
pair for under 10,000 yen.

123
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:04,380
That's okay.

124
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:09,080
These are... the only pair I need!

125
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:15,750
I understand!

126
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:18,380
I'll take on the responsibility
and make sure they get fixed!

127
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,790
Ouch...!

128
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:25,830
Um... I think I'd prefer 
your dad handled them...

129
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:26,790
R-right.

130
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:28,540
Oh, but...

131
00:07:28,710 --> 00:07:29,710
Do you mind,

132
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:32,170
if I gave you just one piece of advice?

133
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:35,580
You should at least change the insoles.

134
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:42,670
Your play style is more focused on speed
than power, Kurumatani.

135
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:50,080
So, it would be best if you could raise the ankle height
to make it more compatible with your quickness.

136
00:07:54,170 --> 00:07:57,250
They sell a lot of that type 
of basketball shoe now,

137
00:07:57,460 --> 00:08:00,080
but if you'd prefer to keep 
the ones you have currently,

138
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:02,670
then there are a few ways
you can customize them for the better.

139
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:04,880
Wow, that's neat.

140
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:06,460
I didn't know they had stuff like this.

141
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:09,960
But wait, how did you know
that my play style focuses on speed?

142
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:12,830
Well, that's really simple.

143
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:15,380
Your looks say it all!

144
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:19,170
Oh... yeah...

145
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,380
Okay then, we'll take 
good care of your shoes.

146
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,630
I think it will take about 10 days for us
to make the repairs...

147
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,380
Huh? 10 whole days?!

148
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,750
In the meantime, I'll let you borrow
the pair that I always use.

149
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:38,420
Wow, a perfect fit. Thanks...

150
00:08:38,710 --> 00:08:42,130
It just kills me that girls' shoes 
are always the right size...

151
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,580
Just one more thing... I owe you an apology.

152
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:46,290
Huh? For what?

153
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:49,250
I lied to you about something I said earlier.

154
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:50,000
You lied?

155
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:54,830
The truth is I was there in the gym,
watching your match with Maru High.

156
00:08:55,250 --> 00:08:57,710
You were so cool, Kurumatani!

157
00:09:11,170 --> 00:09:13,960
Do your best out on the court! Goodnight!

158
00:09:16,540 --> 00:09:18,580
G-goodnight...

159
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:28,790
Is this for real?!

160
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:31,790
Does that girl have the hots for me or what?!

161
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:35,920
No, no, wait a second. Thinking I'm cool
doesn't instantly mean she likes me.

162
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,790
I'm too inexperienced to be
jumping to conclusions, anyway.

163
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:41,670
But then, why was she getting all blushy?!
I saw the red in her cheeks!

164
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:44,500
Actually, the real problem is...

165
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:48,750
...how am I supposed to choose
between her and Madoka?!

166
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,790
Hey, Granny...

167
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:54,540
What's wrong?

168
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:56,630
Can you tell me what "love" really is?

169
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:59,920
Stop acting like such a ninny!
Take a bath and get to bed already!

170
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,290
I can't sleep...

171
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:42,630
Tomorrow... or I guess it's today now,
we're supposed to have a school assembly.

172
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:46,330
I'll just go late...

173
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:00,830
I'm sorry! I was asleep all day!

174
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:05,040
You're late, Kurumatani.

175
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,710
It's already past the time 
for practice to start!

176
00:11:09,130 --> 00:11:09,960
Huh?

177
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:14,170
Okay, guys! Let's put our 
best into practice today!

178
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,880
Yeah!

179
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,290
First, we start with proper warm-ups!

180
00:11:20,750 --> 00:11:23,500
What's gotten into Chiaki and the others?

181
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,420
Well, just take a look.

182
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:26,790
Huh?

183
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,380
Ow, ow, ow...

184
00:11:45,630 --> 00:11:47,380
Hey, Kurumatani!

185
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:50,250
WHAAAAT?!

186
00:11:53,330 --> 00:11:55,880
I'm Nao Nanao! From class 1-3!

187
00:11:56,330 --> 00:11:59,960
I'm 144 centimeters tall, 
and I weigh 36 kilograms!

188
00:12:00,210 --> 00:12:03,630
I'm a Pisces with a B blood type.
And I love green tea pudding!

189
00:12:04,170 --> 00:12:08,460
Although I may not be the best manager,
I will do my utmost to support the team!

190
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,420
I hope we can get along!

191
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:13,290
Nanao is... going to be our manager?

192
00:12:13,290 --> 00:12:14,750
She's so tiny!

193
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:16,170
But super cute.

194
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:18,830
Th-thank God I chose to 
be on the basketball team!

195
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:23,750
Oh my... she's just like a baby chick.

196
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,750
If you're sharing, I'd love to hear
your body measurements...

197
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,250
Sure! From the top, 71, 5-

198
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:30,130
Stop! Stop!

199
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:31,710
Don't ask sleazy questions like those!

200
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:32,880
And don't answer them!

201
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,130
Why pick us?

202
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:36,000
Huh?

203
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,540
There's plenty of other 
teams looking for a manager.

204
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:40,380
So why basketball?

205
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,290
M-my reason is...

206
00:12:45,210 --> 00:12:46,170
Be...

207
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:50,170
Because I like basketball.

208
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,210
She looked at me!

209
00:12:54,670 --> 00:12:55,630
And...

210
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:58,170
SHE WAS BLUSHING!

211
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:14,210
Is it a sign? It has to be!

212
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:16,790
The path to happiness has 
finally opened to me!

213
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:20,000
THIS IS IT!

214
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,460
What's going on with him?

215
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,880
Just ignore it.

216
00:13:24,290 --> 00:13:26,290
He flips out like that a few times a year.

217
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:29,500
Say, Kurumatani?

218
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:31,750
This morning...

219
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:35,210
...why didn't you show up 
to the school assembly?

220
00:13:36,130 --> 00:13:38,330
Did you get sick all of a sudden?

221
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:43,420
U-uh, no, actually... I'm going through
a phase of puberty or something like that...

222
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:45,710
So I was just asleep the whole day...

223
00:13:46,830 --> 00:13:47,670
Kurumatani.

224
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:51,580
You skipped every class today,
yet still showed up for practice.

225
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,460
Consequences must not scare you.

226
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:55,210
Uh, I'm sorry!

227
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:58,250
I'm assuming that you have a VERY
convincing reason for all of this, Kurumatani.

228
00:13:58,250 --> 00:13:59,460
Huh? Th-the reason...?

229
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:01,080
Let's hear it, Kurumatani.

230
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,130
Well, you see...

231
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:04,170
Let's do this!

232
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,630
I'm on fire today!

233
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:07,540
Yasu!

234
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:08,830
Shit!

235
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:14,580
Wow!

236
00:14:17,210 --> 00:14:18,210
Learn to shoot!

237
00:14:18,210 --> 00:14:20,130
A-amazing.

238
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:23,130
I couldn't tell how he managed
to get that pass through the defense!

239
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:29,830
What are you doing? It's 
time to switch sides!

240
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,750
I'm too sweaty now.

241
00:14:31,750 --> 00:14:34,380
But we just started practice a minute ago!

242
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:38,080
Rebound!

243
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:48,040
Wow! That's awesome!

244
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,500
You jump so high! Just like in the NBA!

245
00:14:52,290 --> 00:14:54,710
Of course. That's how we roll.

246
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:57,330
You're turning into somebody else, Momoharu.

247
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:03,960
I'm not letting you get away, dammit!

248
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:13,290
He's fast! And smooth!

249
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,460
He was pulling so many moves in mid-air!

250
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:20,540
I think he might be kind of cool.

251
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:21,460
Huh?!

252
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,750
That's not the reaction that we got!

253
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,960
What're you so enraptured by?

254
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,670
Ow, ow, ow...

255
00:16:09,210 --> 00:16:10,580
Are you okay?

256
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:14,080
Oh, hey, Madoka!

257
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:15,040
Long time no see.

258
00:16:17,290 --> 00:16:18,040
Yay!

259
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,710
I've missed you so much!

260
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:25,880
You're just as tiny as ever, Nao.

261
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:29,880
Never mind me, you've become even more beautiful
since the last time I saw you!

262
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,670
Wish that were me... So lucky.

263
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,630
What's the deal? You old friends?

264
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:36,080
Oh, yeah.

265
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,540
Since back in middle school.

266
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,460
She was the manager for 
the team that I was on.

267
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,880
I owe you so much for all the help
you gave me back then.

268
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,290
Oh, no problem. Same goes for me.

269
00:16:48,290 --> 00:16:50,420
What's up with this weird vibe?

270
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:53,000
Here!

271
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:57,670
Stop! Stop!

272
00:16:58,130 --> 00:16:59,630
No more! That's enough!

273
00:16:59,630 --> 00:17:01,750
Your reaction time after receiving 
a pass is way too slow.

274
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:05,330
If you get the ball when you're in shooting range,
the first thing you should do is look at the basket.

275
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:06,880
Even just a quick glance is okay.

276
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:09,000
Oh, I get it. We're doing 
it to fake them out, right?

277
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,880
Nah. It's to show the defense
that you're serious about trying to score.

278
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,830
Oh! That makes sense.

279
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,630
Sometimes it does lead 
to you faking them out.

280
00:17:17,630 --> 00:17:19,540
Just don't forget to do it, okay?

281
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:22,170
Okay, roger that.

282
00:17:22,170 --> 00:17:24,080
That's great advice, Kite!

283
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,580
I see. You're going to be the 
manager for the boys' team.

284
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:28,080
He's right! No matter what the circumstance,
it's important to always lay on pressure!

285
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,080
So, how are they?

286
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,630
Okay! Let's keep that in mind and try one more time!

287
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,630
Now that you've seen them in action,
what are your thoughts?

288
00:17:30,630 --> 00:17:33,920
W-well... everyone on the team is amazing.

289
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:37,960
I don't think there are many teams out there
with players of this caliber!

290
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,500
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING?!

291
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,670
Please take practice more seriously!

292
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:43,960
Although...

293
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:49,290
I don't think this team stands
any chance of winning actual games.

294
00:17:50,750 --> 00:17:51,630
Huh?

295
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:55,080
Uh, do you think there's 
something holding them back?

296
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:56,380
Well, yes.

297
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,170
Don't be stupid!

298
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:01,210
What makes you such a prophet
after watching us practice for 5 minutes?

299
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,290
You think you know this game 
better than we do, girly?

300
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,250
If that's what she thinks, 
then there's no mistake.

301
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:07,380
Huh?

302
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,000
I can guarantee that personally.

303
00:18:13,330 --> 00:18:15,380
If you'd like, we can even 
prove it with a game.

304
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,960
You can play against our girls' team.

305
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,790
What?!

306
00:18:18,790 --> 00:18:19,630
Why?!

307
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:22,290
A game against the girls' basketball team...?

308
00:18:22,630 --> 00:18:23,960
Hold on, Madoka!

309
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:27,170
Why on Earth would we ever agree
to put ourselves through that?!

310
00:18:27,170 --> 00:18:29,540
Why not? I don't see the problem with it.

311
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:32,580
Oh, come on! Just take one 
good look at those guys!

312
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:35,790
You know they'd foul us
just to grab our butts and chests!

313
00:18:35,790 --> 00:18:39,130
It wouldn't take them much to knock us down
and then who knows what would happen!

314
00:18:39,130 --> 00:18:42,040
Hm. That's a rather brilliant strategy.

315
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,210
No, it's really not.

316
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:46,880
To be honest, I've been wanting
to go up against them for a while now.

317
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:50,670
I mean, don't you ever get tired
of practicing the same stuff every day?

318
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,130
We should take a break to play sometimes!

319
00:18:53,290 --> 00:18:56,130
But we just played an official 
game not too long ago...

320
00:18:56,290 --> 00:18:56,830
Oh yeah.

321
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,290
That reminds me. How did your team do
in the tournament prelims...?

322
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:04,000
We totally lost. In the very first round.

323
00:19:05,130 --> 00:19:06,580
This is a waste of time.

324
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:11,420
It's not worth the effort to play against a girls'
team that can't even put up a fight.

325
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:16,290
I never said that this match 
has to be win or lose.

326
00:19:16,290 --> 00:19:17,130
Huh?

327
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:23,000
It's a good opportunity for you to test your skills
and find out if Nao's assessment is accurate or not.

328
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,040
You don't even have to bother 
with winning or losing.

329
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:29,000
That's all the more reason not to.

330
00:19:30,330 --> 00:19:33,210
None of us are interested
in playing a game that has no stakes.

331
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:37,210
Especially since we'd be playing 
against a bunch of girls.

332
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:39,630
I just can't bring myself 
to take it seriously.

333
00:19:39,630 --> 00:19:41,880
It would just be a waste of time.

334
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,710
You said it.

335
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:44,380
However!

336
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:47,040
Well, we could be convinced.

337
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:52,290
If the girls agree to strip naked when we win,
then I think we could find the motivation!

338
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:56,380
Gotta put a carrot on the stick, so to speak!

339
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:59,710
Isn't that even more of a waste of time
than normal practice?

340
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,830
Very well, then.

341
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:03,380
That's fine.

342
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,750
O..oh-ho?

343
00:20:07,170 --> 00:20:09,580
All the loser has to do is strip down
to the nude, is that right?

344
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:12,250
W-w-wait a second! What are you saying?!

345
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:13,790
Then we're all agreed.

346
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:17,290
Madoka will be the one to do it.

347
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:18,210
What?

348
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:29,580
Then we'll play! Without holding back!

349
00:20:29,790 --> 00:20:30,330
Okay!

350
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:31,040
All right!

351
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:31,750
Hi-yah!

352
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:32,460
Wa-tah!

353
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,880
They're already in position to play!

354
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:41,040
Hold up, Nao. Why's it gotta be me?

355
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:45,080
Oh well, I thought that you were the one
pushing to have a game against them, Madoka!

356
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:48,000
Don't worry.

357
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,790
Just leave it all to me!

358
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:52,540
Owie!

359
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:53,500
I'm sorry.

360
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,670
I'm just not comfortable leaving
my whole future in your hands.

361
00:20:57,790 --> 00:21:00,580
Ow... ow... ouchies...

362
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,580
Hold on, Momoharu!

363
00:21:00,790 --> 00:21:03,670
You're their captain,
so say something to calm them down!

364
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:22,170
The hell was that?! What is happening?!

365
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:24,540
Well, there's no turning back now.

366
00:21:24,710 --> 00:21:28,170
All we can do at this point
is put everything we have into winning.

367
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:31,000
You guys...!

368
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,080
But in exchange...

369
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:34,830
...this is all on you if we lose.

370
00:21:52,790 --> 00:21:54,130
Um, okay then.

371
00:21:54,330 --> 00:21:58,710
Starting now, the game between the boys' and girls'
basketball teams will officially begin!

372
00:21:58,710 --> 00:22:00,960
ALL RIGHT!

373
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:18,710
Doredake sora o miagetatte

374
00:22:18,710 --> 00:22:22,000
Boku wa tobenai to kimi wa itta

375
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,210
Ato nankai te o nobaseba

376
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:28,580
Todoku no darou to naita yoru

377
00:22:28,710 --> 00:22:32,080
Nigedasu koto ni nareteitte

378
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:35,380
Sore ga yowasa dato shitta ano hi

379
00:22:35,380 --> 00:22:39,580
Hajimeyou mata, kyou kara

380
00:22:42,210 --> 00:22:48,210
Taisetsu na mono wa itsudemo soba ni atta

381
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:54,540
Bokura wa itsumo hitori janai donna toki mo

382
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:57,880
Toberu sa doko made mo kimi wa

383
00:22:57,880 --> 00:23:01,630
Dare yori tataku tataku habataite

384
00:23:01,830 --> 00:23:05,880
Nagashita namida no kazu dake

385
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,830
Tsuyoku narunda

386
00:23:07,830 --> 00:23:11,210
Tsubasa hiroge sekai o megutte

387
00:23:11,210 --> 00:23:14,790
Dare mo shiranai mirai o sagasou

388
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:19,380
Zutto, zutto, zutto

389
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:23,040
Aruite yukou saa, issho ni

390
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Boys' Stubborness
and the Girls' Pride

391
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:35,130
Next time: "The Boys' Stubbornness 
